    more: "UBC-GIF or contractor inversions, and block models exported from Datamine, Micromine, Surpac, Vulcan or Leapfrog. Each loaded model gets a card with its colours, range, opacity and exports; Targeting > Voxel ranges isolates value ranges, and a model can be evaluated onto the drillholes and reported. A UBC dcinv3d / ipinv3d result (.msh with .con, .res or .chg, or an X, Y, Z, value CSV) loads here; only raw station or electrode readings go to Point survey or DC / IP. OMF files (Leapfrog, Seequent) have their own pane, Open Mining Format; export a VTK or Geosoft model as a UBC mesh and model, or as a block-model CSV.",
